# Shell scripts are LF everywhere, whatever core.autocrlf says locally.
#
# Two things run them and both break on a CR: the box, where a shebang
# ending "bash\r" fails with "bad interpreter", and the test suite, which
# executes bin/deploy and friends through Git Bash on Windows. Without this
# a fresh clone on a machine with autocrlf=true checks them out with CRLF
# and the failure names the interpreter rather than the line endings.
bin/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
